<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>At NAB's scale</strong>,=
 I'd recommend <strong>LRU with frequency-aware TTL adjustment</strong> bec=
ause banking searches have both temporal patterns (recent payees) and frequ=
ency patterns (common operations), plus the regulatory requirement for data=
 freshness in financial contexts.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Th=
at hybrid approach is really thoughtful. You mentioned regulatory requireme=
nts - that's crucial in banking. How would you handle cache invalidation wh=
en dealing with real-time financial data updates? For instance, if a user's=
 account balance changes due to an external transaction, how do you ensure =
cache coherency across multiple browser tabs or devices?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: This=
 is one of the most critical challenges in fintech applications, and NAB's =
scale makes it even more complex. We need to think about <strong>distribute=
d cache coherency</strong> with <strong>strong consistency guarantees</stro=
ng> for financial accuracy.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>My approach involves mul=
tiple layers of cache invalidation:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1. Server-Sent Events (S=
SE) for real-time invalidation:</strong></p>
