<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Key Insights for NAB Imp=
lementation:</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Cancellation timing is =
critical</strong> - too early breaks user flows, too late wastes resources<=
/li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Resource cleanup must b=
e atomic and guaranteed</strong> - no partial cleanups in financial systems=
</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory management is pa=
ramount</strong> - banking apps run for extended periods</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Audit trails are essent=
ial</strong> - regulatory compliance requires tracking all operations</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Fallback strategies are=
 mandatory</strong> - cancellation itself can fail and needs handling</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This foundation sets us up perfe=
ctly for implementing the <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 bo=
rder-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 p=
y-px text-[0.9rem]">Promise.cancelable</code> utility with production-grade=
 robustness.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
cellent analysis! Your approach to resource management and audit trails sho=
ws you understand the regulatory environment we operate in. The batch cance=
llation optimization is particularly thoughtful for our scale.</p>
