celable</code> that can wrap any promise and provide a <code class=3D"bg-te=
xt-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre=
-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">.cancel()</code> method. B=
ut I want to see how you'd approach this from first principles. What are th=
e different implementation strategies you'd consider, and what are the trad=
e-offs of each approach?</p>
